# Current theses

## Thesis T-six-command-root: Adopt the six-command CLI contract
Status: accepted
Based-on: user:decision
Supersedes: T-migrated-root

### Guidance
<folder_context path=".">
<application_context name="git-a2a schema 2">
git-a2a is a cross-platform Git component dependency manager. A dependency combines code,
one responsible external agent, and an optional published surface. The CLI applies code through
consumer-platform adapters and exposes metadata for an external A2A client; it never sends A2A
messages, runs agents, hosts endpoints, or manages tasks.
</application_context>
<system_invariant name="six domain commands">
The only domain commands are init, add, pull, remove, list, and whose. --help and --version are service
flags. Do not add aliases or reintroduce install, update, restore, show, validate, status, who,
contact, card, catalog, trust, setup, mcp, upgrade, wire, fetch, sync, doctor, pin, or authoring
commands.
</system_invariant>
<settled_decision name="schema 2 files">
The root declaration is exactly one of a2amodule.yml or a2amodule.yaml; generators write .yml.
The lock is a2amodule.lock and local recoverable state is under ignored .git-a2a/. Schema 1 is
rejected before mutation and has no compatibility reader or migrate command.
</settled_decision>
<settled_decision name="component ownership">
A manifest declares one component and at most one responsible external agent. The agent is an
A2A Agent Card reference, not duplicated skills, interfaces, authentication, roles, scopes,
intents, contacts, trust policy, or liveness state. An incomplete manifest created by init may
omit the agent; an upstream used by add or pull must declare agent.card.
</settled_decision>
<settled_decision name="direct dependencies and revision">
Dependencies are direct and consumer-local aliases. Add resolves an omitted ref to the actual
default branch. Pull resolves the requested branch, tag, or commit once; every polyglot binding,
the upstream manifest, and surface use that same commit. The selected adapter and concrete
variant are durable in the declaration and lock and must never change because PATH or marker
files changed. Lock is written only after a successful per-dependency transaction.
</settled_decision>
<settled_decision name="surface">
Surface is optional upstream tracked data and is not installation. A declared relative directory
or '.' is materialized from the applied commit under .git-a2a/surfaces/ALIAS. Exclude .git,
untracked files, traversal, and symlink escape. Missing surface means no published source access.
</settled_decision>
<settled_decision name="adapter matrix">
Preserve every real adapter in adapters/: npm-family, Python, Go, Cargo, Swift, Pub, Gem,
Composer, Hex, Hackage, Zig, Clojure, Nix, CMake, Gradle, MSBuild, Maven, and Meson. Git submodule
is an ordinary registry adapter. Build adapters compose with one submodule materialization and
must not recreate vendor/copy subsystems. Unsupported native Git sources fall back explicitly to
submodule; a missing executable never silently changes a saved adapter.
</settled_decision>
<critical_system_mandates name="safe mutation">
Preflight conflicts, tools, and dirty submodules before mutation. Never erase user changes.
Snapshot and roll back owned manifests, native lockfiles, and Git metadata on failure; report
unrecoverable external cache state precisely. Pass remote data as argv/data, never shell code.
</critical_system_mandates>
<approved_dependency_whitelist name="Go runtime">
gopkg.in/yaml.v3 is the only non-standard-library runtime dependency. Do not use CGO.
</approved_dependency_whitelist>
<compilation_and_testing_pipeline>
Keep go build ./..., go test ./..., go vet ./..., race tests, schema/examples parity, adapter
corpus, conformance, docs/site checks, and darwin/linux/windows amd64/arm64 cross-builds green.
Native execution claims require that native runtime; cross-compilation is build evidence only.
</compilation_and_testing_pipeline>
<scope_boundary name="distribution">
Keep binary installation and packaging channels, removing only MCP/setup/self-updater artifacts.
Do not publish a release, create a stable tag, or deploy the site without a separate request.
</scope_boundary>
</folder_context>

### Rationale
The user directly replaced the five-command surface with the six-command list/whose contract.
